; THE GLACIER PASS (the 2026-08-28 layout rebuild) - a 60 x 20 corridor north of the clan hold, and a DEAD END:
; the hold is the only cell that touches it, at its southern edge. It is somewhere you climb into and
; come back out of, so it is built as one route with two pockets rather than as a through-road.
;
; WARNING WHAT THIS REPLACED. Two ice masses at the centre and four more in mirrored pairs at
; x = +/-18..24, leaving a straight eight-metre lane down the middle. The comment called it a
; compressed corridor; walked, it was a wide flat strip with scenery either side of it.
;
; THE ROUTE NOW WEAVES. You enter from the hold at (0, 10) and the ice alternates north and south -
; (-6, -6), (4, 6), (-16, -6), (16, 6), (-24, 5), (24, -5) - with the two rock masses filling the
; gaps at (-11, 7) and (11, -7). The walkable line is never straight for more than about twelve
; metres and never narrower than six, which is inside the 0.5 m navmesh agent radius with room for a
; mount. The two ends are pockets, not exits: west past (-24, 5) and east past (24, -5).

